.TH PKGBUILD 1 "2026-09-07" "@PROJECT_NAME@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pkgbuild \- build an Emerald port package
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkgbuild
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ port ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pkgbuild
fetches, verifies, extracts, builds, and packages a port according to its build script. Depending on options it can stop after downloading or extraction, install the result, or generate package metadata. Build and cache paths come from the configuration unless overridden.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -q, --quiet
Show only status messages and errors.
.TP
.B -i, --install
Install the resulting package.
.TP
.B -u, --upgrade
Install as an upgrade.
.TP
.B -r, --reinstall
Reinstall the resulting package.
.TP
.B -c, --ignore-conflict
Ignore installation conflicts.
.TP
.B -v, --verbose
Show verbose installation output.
.TP
.B -f, --force-rebuild
Rebuild even if a package is already available.
.TP
.B -m, --skip-checksum
Skip checksum verification.
.TP
.B -g, --gen-checksum
Generate a checksum for the source.
.TP
.B -o, --download
Download source only.
.TP
.B -x, --extract
Download and extract source only.
.TP
.B -p, --pkgfiles
Generate the package file list.
.TP
.B -w, --keep-work
Keep the working directory.
.TP
.B -C, --clean
Remove downloaded sources and prebuilt packages.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help.
.TP
.B --config=FILE
Use a custom configuration file.
.TP
.B --srcdir=PATH
Override the source cache directory.
.TP
.B --pkgdir=PATH
Override the package cache directory.
.TP
.B --workdir=PATH
Override the working directory.
.TP
.B --jobs=N
Override parallel build jobs; by default uses JOBS or the number of processors.
.TP
.B --no-backup
Do not back up configuration files during an upgrade.
.SH FILES
A port normally contains the configured build script (default \fB@BUILD_SCRIPT@\fR), \fB@CHECKSUMS_FILE@\fR, and \fB@PKGFILES_FILE@\fR as applicable.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success; non-zero on failed fetch, checksum, build, packaging, or installation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkgadd (1),
.BR portcreate (1),
.BR @PROJECT_NAME@.conf (5)
